commit 74b3131d0ab0da1f63c3798040437410c1909849
Author: иван гужов <mac@Mac-mini-ivan.local>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 08:06:06 2026 +0300

    core: cancellation, progress, and pipeline hardening; chunked ffmpeg mix for long videos
    
    Add stage-level cancellation and retry (cancellation.py, pipeline.py), in-stage
    progress parsing (progress.py), and exact engine-adapter inputs with a per-stage
    parameter hash. Track core/app/models explicitly: an unanchored "models/" rule
    had silently excluded the package, so clones could not import the core.
    
    Mix audio in chunks sized from the real fd cap instead of one monolithic ffmpeg
    call: a 24-min video means 543 inputs, which blew past the 256-descriptor macOS
    terminal limit (exit 232 / EMFILE). Verified at ulimit 64 and 256; add tests and
    a core-vs-cli comparison tool with its evidence logs.
    
